# The SIR model of an epidemic
# Susceptible people s catch the disease from infected ones i, who then
# recover (r). The outbreak grows while each case infects more than one
# other, that is while s > gamma/beta (Kermack and McKendrick, 1927).
s'=-beta*s*i
i'=beta*s*i-gamma*i
r'=gamma*i
par beta=0.5,gamma=0.2
init s=0.999,i=0.001,r=0
@ total=100,dt=0.05,meth=rungekutta
@ xp=t,yp=i,xlo=0,xhi=100,ylo=0,yhi=1
done
